# Legacy wiivolve.com links (2006-2008) -> the archived page. Contract: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, section 7.4.
# Parsed by Cloudflare at deploy time and never served.
#
# Verified with wrangler 4.157.0 dev (the same asset-worker code that runs at the edge): when a
# destination has no query string of its own, the incoming query string is appended, so
#   /cheats.php?alpha=a  ->  https://web.archive.org/web/2008/http://wiivolve.com/cheats.php?alpha=a
# Matching is on the path only, exact and case-sensitive. Static rules are checked before
# dynamic (splat) rules; among dynamic rules the first match wins.
#
# Not here on purpose: the endpoints with an id (fullNews.php, article.php, review.php, preview.php,
# gameInfo.php, cheat.php) and a "/*.php" catch-all. Those requests get site/404.html (status 404), and
# its 404.js sends a documented post, feature, review or preview, or a captured game or cheat page, to
# its best capture (site/legacy-map.json; 188 of the 220 posts have no capture of their own), an id the
# map does not know to the old site's own list for that endpoint, and any other old .php page to the 2008
# form. A catch-all here would answer those endpoints first, in every spelling. tests/hosting.test.mjs
# checks this.
#
# 302, not 301, for the archive: browsers keep a 301 without Cache-Control for good, and the best
# archive address for a page can change.

# New homes for two old endpoints.
